<ol class="notes">
  <li><span><b>Stored first, notified second.</b> The inquiry endpoint, the only public PHP, writes to MariaDB before anything else. Email is only a notification; a failed send shows "Retry", and the dashboard badge never depends on email.</span></li>
  <li><span><b>Workflow:</b> new → in progress → answered → closed. Each change is an AuditEvent, and the tab counts are the work queue.</span></li>
  <li><span><b>Automatic code matching</b> with the shared normaliser: aliases resolve to their product. Unmatched codes are flagged and feed the dashboard's "not in catalogue" list (C4). Nothing is logged about visitors who did not write to you.</span></li>
  <li><span><b>One-tap reply channels:</b> WhatsApp (wa.me) and phone (tel:) are built from the stored number, which is displayed in Latin digits (Q2). There are no price fields or quote documents; pricing stays an offline conversation.</span></li>
  <li><span><b>Never published:</b> inquiries exist only in the database and its backups, never in a release. Retention and deletion-on-request rules are set in Phase 3.</span></li>
  <li><span><b>The mobile view (A9)</b> covers triage on the phone: read, call or WhatsApp, change status.</span></li>
</ol>
{% endcall %}

