      <div class="r2">{% for c in q.codes %}<span class="code">{{ c[0] }}</span>{% if not c[1] %} <span class="badge b-pend">خارج از کاتالوگ</span>{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class="phone">
    <div class="phone__top"><span>→</span><b class="code" style="font-weight:600">IQ-1027</b><span class="badge b-new">جدید</span></div>
    <div class="inq__detail">
      <dl class="kv"><dt>نام</dt><dd>مشتری نمونه ۱ · شرکت نمونه</dd><dt>تلفن</dt><dd><span class="num">0912 XXX XXXX</span></dd><dt>دریافت</dt><dd>امروز ۱۰:۰۵ · فارسی</dd></dl>
      <div class="msg" style="font-size:14px">سلام. برای یک خط تولید به ۴۰ عدد <span class="code">6205-2RS</span> و ۱۰ عدد <span class="code">6208</span> نیاز داریم…</div>
      <div style="display:grid;gap:6px;font-size:13.5px"><span><span class="code">6205-2RS</span> ← <span class="good">6205 ✓</span></span><span><span class="code">6208</span> ← <span class="badge b-pend">در کاتالوگ نیست</span></span></div>
      <div class="field"><span class="lbl">وضعیت</span><span class="a-sel">جدید</span></div>
      <span class="a-ta is-ph">یادداشت داخلی…</span>
    </div>
    <div class="phone__bar"><span class="a-btn a-btn--ok">واتس‌اپ</span><span class="a-btn">تماس</span></div>
  </div>
</div>
<ol class="notes">
  <li><span><b>Thumb-reachable actions:</b> WhatsApp and Call sit in a fixed bottom bar with 46 px targets, and status is a single select.</span></li>
  <li><span><b>Same data, same rules</b> as A6: code matching, audit events, and no price fields.</span></li>
  <li><span><b>Product, Sections and Publish screens</b> stay usable on a phone (single-column reflow) but are not optimised for it. This keeps the admin small and fast.</span></li>
</ol>
{% endcall %}

<section class="doc-sec" id="model" aria-labelledby="h-model">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="h-model">Entity → screen map</h2>
    <p>Every entity of the Stage 0 content model (section H) has a home. Screens not drawn here (Families, Sources, Brands, Documents, SEO overview, Users, Audit log, Backups) reuse the same two patterns: the dense list (A2) and the form with a side panel (A3/A8).</p>
    <div class="map-scroll"><table class="map">
      <thead><tr><th>Entity</th><th>Edited in</th><th>Also surfaces in</th><th>Key rule</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for e in entity_map %}<tr><td>{{ e[0] }}</td><td>{{ e[1] }}</td><td>{{ e[2] }}</td><td>{{ e[3] }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="doc-sec" id="standards" aria-labelledby="h-std" style="background:var(--sheet);border-top:1px solid var(--rule)">
  <div class="wrap cols2">
    <div>
      <h2 id="h-std">Admin UX standards</h2>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li><b>Inline validation</b> next to the field, with save feedback and an unsaved-change guard.</li>
        <li><b>Confirmation dialogs</b> only for destructive or public actions (archive, delete, restore, rollback, publish).</li>
        <li><b>Every list has an empty state and an error state</b>; empty states explain the next step (e.g. "No inquiries yet — they arrive from the site form").</li>
        <li><b>Persian UI, RTL, Vazirmatn</b>; codes, dimensions, units, phone numbers and release IDs are always Latin JetBrains Mono; ordinary counts use Persian digits.</li>
        <li><b>Minimum label size 13 px</b>, 34 px controls (46 px on touch), visible focus ring, full keyboard operation, WCAG 2.2 AA contrast.</li>
        <li><b>Server-rendered PHP pages with a little vanilla JS</b> (tabs, chips, upload progress). No SPA framework; admin assets live under <span class="mono">/admin</span> and are never referenced by public pages.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Open questions for Gate 2</h2>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li><b>English admin UI?</b> Recommended: no for v1 (Persian only), since content is still edited in both languages. Confirm.</li>
        <li><b>Who verifies?</b> Proposed: only the Owner can set "Verified for indexing". Confirm, or allow Editors.</li>
        <li><b>Inquiry notification address</b> and SMTP availability (host probe) are needed before launch.</li>
        <li><b>CSV import</b> of the existing catalogue: confirm we should plan it (needs the old catalogue export).</li>
        <li><b>Admin dark mode:</b> not planned (scope). The public site follows the device setting, as approved in Q1.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</main>
<footer class="foot"><div class="wrap">Polad Charkhesh Nova · Phase 2 V2 · Admin wireframes for Gate 2 review · placeholders are labelled; no production code, schema or Publish Engine exists yet.</div></footer>
</body>
</html>
